{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LowestCommonAncestors","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For vertices at preorder positions p < q, the answer is the vertex at the least position among"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the parents of the vertices at positions p + 1 … q: those parents lie in the answer’s subtree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and include it, and it has the least position there. So a query is one range minimum over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"n − 1 parent positions (the Euler tour reduction on half the entries), answered by 64-entry"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"blocks with a bitmask of each prefix’s minimum stack and a sparse table over the blocks’ minima."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"About two words per vertex, plus (n\/64)·log₂(n\/64) for the table."}]}]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms"]]},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14TreeAlgorithms21LowestCommonAncestorsV","title":"LowestCommonAncestors","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"LowestCommonAncestors"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LowestCommonAncestors"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struc